  "title": "Coast Guard Auxiliary Helps Rescue Kemp's Ridley Turtles (no audio)",
  "description": "Coast Guard Auxiliary pilots along with members from the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Association and the New England Aquarium helped rescue 25 Kemp's Ridley Turtles from the cold waters of Cape Cod to Florida Thursday. January, 7, 2016. The turtles became trapped in the arm of Cape Cod on their journey to warmer water for the winter. U.S. Coast Guard video by Petty Officer 3rd Class Ross Ruddell. *NOTE: There is no audio with this video.**",
